208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Intro to the topic:  A new development in the field of adaptive optics \(AO\) on ground-based telescopes enables routine monitoring of changes on Jupiter's volcanic moon Io at scales down to ~80km \(achieved\), or even down to ~50km \(in the limit\). Our observations of Io, taken with SHARK-VIS on the Large Binocular Telescope \(LBT\) in Arizona, demonstrate this new capability. SHARK-VIS, which saw first light at LBT on October 2nd, 2023, is one of only a few visible-light AO instruments on large telescopes.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
